{# The foot of an entry — onward reading and authorship.

   Shared by layouts/post.njk and layouts/digesting.njk. It lived inline in
   post.njk, which meant digesting entries had a byline and nothing else: no
   related entries, no rail, no way forward or back once you had landed on one
   from a link. Extracting it is what stops the two layouts drifting apart
   again.

   Feedback sits at the end of the reading column in the calling layout. This
   full-width block begins only after that question, when attention shifts to
   what to read next and who wrote the piece.

   Two columns: onward links on the left, authorship on the right.

   The DOM follows the desktop columns from left to right, so keyboard tab
   order and screen-reader order agree with what is on screen. At narrower
   widths the same two units stack without CSS reordering.

   Pages with no entry carry a short blurb in the footer instead -- see
   footer.njk. The homepage has neither, because the hero says it. #}
<div class="kh-stack kh-u-padding__top--800" data-pagefind-ignore>
  {%- if page.url != '/privacy/' %}

  <div class="kh-entry-foot kh-u-do-not-print">
    {#- No wrapper heading. "Read next / By meaning, and in sequence" sat
        directly above "Closest in meaning / By similarity, not by tag" --
        two rules and two straplines for one idea. The related list owns the
        h2; the rail gets an h3 under it. -#}
    <section class="kh-readnext">
      {% include "partials/related-semantic.njk" %}

      {#- The rail is orientation -- where this entry sits in the register --
          rather than a reading list; the related entries above are the reading
          list. Every mark is a link, so the adjacent entries are still one
          click away, which is why the "Previously:" and "Next:" lines that
          used to sit here are gone: they restated two of these marks in prose.
          -#}
      <h3 class="kh-text-heading--3 kh-readnext__seq-head">Read next in sequence</h3>
      {%- set seqNeighbours = collections.allContent | neighbourhood(page.url, 3) %}
      {% include "partials/sequence-mark.njk" %}
    </section>

    {% include "partials/author-note.njk" %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
